---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const phone = '+19255550199';
const phoneDisplay = '(925) 555-0199';
---
<Layout>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="hero-badge">● CONCORD &amp; CONTRA COSTA COUNTY · 24 / 7 EMERGENCY SERVICE</div>
        <h1>WATER HEATER<br />REPAIR IN <span>CONCORD</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">Fast Fixes. Real Relief. Same-Day Service.</p>
        <p class="hero-desc">When your water heater fails in Concord, every cold shower counts. Our licensed technicians are on call around the clock — delivering expert repairs, upfront pricing, and workmanship backed by a written guarantee for every home in Contra Costa County.</p>
        <div class="hero-tags">
          <span class="hero-tag">⏱ Same-Day Response</span>
          <span class="hero-tag">🛡 Licensed &amp; Insured</span>
          <span class="hero-tag">✓ Upfront Pricing</span>
          <span class="hero-tag">📞 24 / 7 Emergency</span>
          <span class="hero-tag">🛡 Workmanship Guarantee</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Schedule an Appointment</a>
          <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-outline">Get a Quote</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <div class="hero-card">
          <div class="hero-card-icon">🚿</div>
          <h3>No Hot Water?</h3>
          <p>We diagnose and repair tank, tankless, gas &amp; electric water heaters the same day in most cases.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why Us -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="why">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Why Concord Homeowners <span>Choose Us</span></h2>
        <p>Concord homes rely on reliable hot water year-round. When your water heater struggles, you need a licensed local specialist who responds the same day and repairs it right the first time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">⚡</div>
          <h3>Same-Day Diagnosis &amp; Repair</h3>
          <p>Most same-day water heater repair calls in Concord are completed within hours of your call — no multi-day waits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">📜</div>
          <h3>Licensed &amp; Certified</h3>
          <p>Every technician is licensed, insured, and trained on tank, tankless, gas, electric, and hybrid systems common in Contra Costa County.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">💵</div>
          <h3>Upfront Pricing, Zero Surprises</h3>
          <p>We quote before we wrench. No hidden fees, no upsell pressure — just honest water heater repair at fair local rates.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">📍</div>
          <h3>Local to Concord</h3>
          <p>Based in Concord — we know the housing stock, common brands (Rheem, A.O. Smith, Bradford White, Rinnai), and seismic strapping requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="stats-row">
        <div class="stat-item"><strong>47 min</strong><span>Avg. Response</span></div>
        <div class="stat-item"><strong>98%</strong><span>First-Visit Fix Rate</span></div>
        <div class="stat-item"><strong>24/7</strong><span>Emergency Available</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Problems preview -->
  <section class="section" id="problems">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Recognize <span>These Signs?</span></h2>
        <p>Hard water and age accelerate water heater wear in Concord. If your system shows any of these symptoms, don't wait.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problems-grid">
        <a href="/problems/no-hot-water/" class="problem-card" style="display:block">
          <span class="problem-badge badge-urgent">Urgent</span>
          <h3>No Hot Water</h3>
          <p>Complete loss of hot water often means a failed element, pilot outage, or tripped breaker. Same-day service restores comfort fast.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/problems/leaking-water-heater/" class="problem-card" style="display:block">
          <span class="problem-badge badge-urgent">Urgent</span>
          <h3>Leaking Water Heater</h3>
          <p>Water pooling around the unit signals a tank leak, loose fitting, or T&amp;P valve issue. Act before floor damage spreads.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/problems/strange-noises/" class="problem-card" style="display:block">
          <span class="problem-badge badge-soon">Address Soon</span>
          <h3>Strange Noises</h3>
          <p>Popping or rumbling usually means sediment. Flushing or anode service can extend tank life significantly.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/problems/inconsistent-temperature/" class="problem-card" style="display:block">
          <span class="problem-badge badge-soon">Address Soon</span>
          <h3>Inconsistent Temperature</h3>
          <p>Hot then cold water points to a failing thermostat, sediment, or undersized unit.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/problems/rusty-water/" class="problem-card" style="display:block">
          <span class="problem-badge badge-urgent">Urgent</span>
          <h3>Rusty or Discolored Water</h3>
          <p>Often a depleted anode or corroding tank. Inspect before full failure.</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/problems/pilot-light-issues/" class="problem-card" style="display:block">
          <span class="problem-badge badge-soon">Address Soon</span>
          <h3>Pilot Light Issues</h3>
          <p>Pilot that won't stay lit is usually a thermocouple — a quick, affordable fix.</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Services preview -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="services">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Expert Water Heater <span>Repair Services</span></h2>
        <p>Every hot-water problem has a root cause. Our certified technicians diagnose accurately and repair correctly.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="services-grid">
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="service-label">Urgent Response</span>
          <h3>Emergency Water Heater Repair</h3>
          <p>When hot water fails at the worst moment, we respond around the clock — no after-hours surcharge surprises.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Available 24 / 7</li>
            <li>Avg. response under 60 min</li>
            <li>Stocked service vehicles</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/emergency-water-heater-repair/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Learn More</a>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="service-label">Most Common</span>
          <h3>Tank Water Heater Repair</h3>
          <p>Gas &amp; electric tank units. Elements, thermostats, anodes, and full diagnostics for all major brands.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>All major brands</li>
            <li>Written estimate first</li>
            <li>Same-visit repairs</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/tank-water-heater-repair/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Learn More</a>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="service-label">Modern Systems</span>
          <h3>Tankless Water Heater Repair</h3>
          <p>Error codes, descaling, ignition and flow sensor repair for Rinnai, Navien, Rheem and more.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Brand specialists</li>
            <li>Descaling &amp; maintenance</li>
            <li>Same-visit when possible</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/tankless-water-heater-repair/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Learn More</a>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="service-label">Critical</span>
          <h3>Leak Detection &amp; Repair</h3>
          <p>Locate the source fast — tank, fittings, or T&amp;P valve — and stop damage before it spreads.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Fast isolation</li>
            <li>Seismic strap check</li>
            <li>Honest repair vs replace</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/leak-detection-repair/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Learn More</a>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="service-label">Preventive</span>
          <h3>Flush &amp; Maintenance</h3>
          <p>Sediment removal and anode inspection extend tank life and lower energy use.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Full tank flush</li>
            <li>Anode inspection</li>
            <li>T&amp;P valve test</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/water-heater-maintenance/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Learn More</a>
        </div>
        <div class="service-card">
          <span class="service-label">Replacement</span>
          <h3>Water Heater Installation</h3>
          <p>Code-compliant tank or tankless installs with proper seismic strapping for California homes.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Same-day installs often available</li>
            <li>Permit guidance</li>
            <li>Workmanship warranty</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/services/water-heater-installation/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">Learn More</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Process -->
  <section class="section" id="process">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>How We Restore <span>Your Hot Water</span></h2>
        <p>Every Concord water heater repair follows a structured, transparent process.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="process-steps">
        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="step-num">01</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Scheduling &amp; Same-Day Response</h3>
            <p>Call or text. We confirm your appointment quickly — often offering same-day slots. We gather a brief symptom overview so the technician arrives prepared.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="step-num">02</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Precision Diagnostic Inspection</h3>
            <p>We test heating elements, thermostats, gas valves, pressure, anode condition, and look for leaks or sediment. Problems are identified with instruments, not assumptions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="step-num">03</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Honest Findings &amp; Repair Options</h3>
            <p>Before any work begins, your technician explains exactly what was found in plain language. You receive a clear written estimate. No pressure.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="step-num">04</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Skilled Repair</h3>
            <p>With your approval, the repair begins. Service vehicles carry common parts so most jobs finish on the first visit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="process-step">
          <div class="step-num">05</div>
          <div>
            <h3>Performance Verification</h3>
            <p>We verify hot water output, check for leaks, confirm thermostat response, and leave you with a post-repair summary.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Map -->
  <section class="section section-alt" id="map">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Find Us in <span>Concord, CA</span></h2>
        <p>Proudly serving Concord and all of Contra Costa County from Richard Avenue.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="map-wrapper">
        <iframe title="Map of 2644 Richard Ave, Concord, CA 94520" src="https://www.openstreetmap.org/export/embed.html?bbox=-122.0532194%2C37.9735961%2C-122.0332194%2C37.9935961&amp;layer=mapnik&amp;marker=37.9835961%2C-122.0432194" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade" allowfullscreen></iframe>
      </div>
      <div class="map-info">
        <h3>📍 2644 Richard Ave, Concord, CA 94520</h3>
        <p>Serving Concord · Pleasant Hill · Walnut Creek · Martinez · Clayton · Pittsburg · Antioch and surrounding communities.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:0.75rem"><a href="/service-areas/" class="btn btn-outline-dark">View All Service Areas</a> &nbsp; <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary">Call {phoneDisplay}</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="cta-banner" id="contact">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Water Heater Down in Concord?</h2>
      <p>Don't suffer through cold showers. If your system stopped working, is leaking, or is making unusual sounds — our team can respond today.</p>
      <a href={`tel:${phone}`} class="btn btn-primary" style="font-size:1.1rem;padding:1rem 2rem">Call Now — {phoneDisplay}</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Water Heater Repair <span>Questions</span></h2>
        <p>Real answers to what Concord homeowners ask most.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>My water heater stopped producing hot water — is this an emergency?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Yes, especially with kids, elderly residents, or medical needs. Most complete failures trace to a tripped breaker, failed element, pilot outage, or thermostat. Emergency calls placed earlier in the day are typically completed same-day.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>How much does water heater repair cost in Concord?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Simple fixes (thermostat, element, thermocouple) often range from a few hundred dollars. We provide a written estimate before any work begins. Replacement is recommended when the unit is old and repair exceeds roughly 50% of replacement cost.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do you repair both tank and tankless water heaters?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Yes. We service traditional tank (gas and electric), tankless, and hybrid units from all major brands including Rheem, A.O. Smith, Bradford White, Rinnai, Navien, and more.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Are you licensed and insured in California?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Yes. All work is performed by licensed, insured technicians familiar with California plumbing codes and seismic strapping requirements for water heaters in Concord and Contra Costa County.</div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Should I repair or replace my water heater?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">Repair usually makes sense if the unit is under 10–12 years old and the issue is isolated. Replacement is worth evaluating for units 12+ years old, recurring failures, or when repair cost approaches half the value of a new system. We give an honest assessment either way.</div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
